verdict PluginLoader: The rewrite, main module and LOADER.get by hash work; tails, PluginLoadError and plugin-named props do not.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/edge-compute/src/plugin-loader/PluginLoader.ts#workerCode, github:dxos/edge/packages/services/compute-service/src/plugins/plugin-router.ts#bundleEntrypoint]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/edge-compute/src/plugin-loader/PluginLoader.test.ts, github:dxos/edge/packages/services/edge/test/plugin-store.node.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The dxos loader rewrites bare imports through vendor/, prunes unreachable vendored files and generates the main module. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/edge-compute/src/plugin-loader/PluginLoader.ts#workerCode
    - compute-service calls LOADER.get with `plugin:<hash>` and binds only space-agnostic services in env. github:dxos/edge/packages/services/compute-service/src/plugins/plugin-router.ts#bundleEntrypoint
  note: |
    The WorkerCode has no `tails`, so a bundle's logs do not reach FunctionsLoggerEntrypoint. The loopback entrypoints
    get empty props, not the plugin's name. A load failure surfaces as the raw Worker Loader error, not as a
    PluginLoadError.
```

